Begin with $U=\boldsymbol 1+\epsilon M+O(\epsilon^2),$ where $\epsilon$ is real and small. Then $U^\dagger=\boldsymbol 1+\epsilon M^\dagger+O(\epsilon^2),$ and unitarity gives $\begin{aligned}
U^\dagger U
 &=\boldsymbol 1+\epsilon(M^\dagger+M)+O(\epsilon^2).\end{aligned}$ To first order, $M^\dagger=-M.$ Thus the matrix $M$ in Equation  is anti-Hermitian.

